  D7: NOT DISTINCT -- route follows LCDM's halo-mass dependence

  GATE D (post-hoc): REDUCES TO LAMBDACDM PLUS A COINCIDENCE
  The only content the route adds to the LambdaCDM comparator is the numerical statement a0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_Lambda) with kappa = 1/2 FITTED; it enters no equation of the class (the class has no acceleration scale: D2's argument), so it is a coincidence the route neither explains nor tests.
  This is a statement about THIS class (a bound early cold fluid with no extra coupling); it is not a statement about candidate B, whose flat a0(z) and tight RAR are what the class does not make.
